 126:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *  This function writes the data to the NVRAM store. It will check the 
 127:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *  appropriate alignment of a start address and also perform an address range 
 128:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *  check based on the length before performing the write operation.
 129:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *  This function performs memory compare and writes only row where there are new
 130:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *  data to write.
 131:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *
 132:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *  \param buffer:   Pointer to the buffer containing the data to be stored.
 133:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *  \param varFlash: Pointer to the array or variable in the flash.
 134:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *  \param length:    The length of the data in bytes.
 135:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *
 136:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** * \return
 137:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *  CYRET_SUCCESS    a successful write
 138:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *  CYRET_BAD_PARAM  A request to write outside the flash boundary.
 139:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *  CYRET_UNKNOWN    Other errors in writing the flash
 140:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *
 141:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** * \sideeffect
 142:Generated_Source\PSoC4/BLE_1_HAL_PVT.c **** *  For BLE devices with 128K of Flash memory this function will automatically 
